"""What an Apple build needs from a Mac, written down instead.

Analyzing an Apple target asks for two things Linux does not have. The cc
toolchains `apple_support` registers declare `exec_compatible_with =
["@platforms//os:macos"]`—"These only execute on macOS"—so toolchain
resolution finds no execution platform to run them on. And `xcode_configure`
writes a `local_config_xcode` holding no Xcode versions at all on a
non-Darwin host, which `rules_swift` reports as "Could not determine Xcode
version at all".

Both are answered by declaring rather than discovering. Nothing here has to
exist on the machine: the fishery only ever runs `aquery`, so an execution
platform is a claim about where actions *would* run, and `xcode_version` is
a Starlark rule that records a version rather than looking for one. The
version below is a fiction, and a fixed one, which is what makes the
recorded report the same on every machine—more stable, in fact, than
recording on a real Mac, where the installed Xcode would vary.

The labels below are canonical repository names, doubled at-sign and all,
which buildifier is right to warn about everywhere else. A repository
injected with `--inject_repository` does not inherit the project's repo
mapping, and `rules_apple` calls this module `build_bazel_apple_support`, so
an apparent name resolves to nothing from in here.
"""

# buildifier: disable=canonical-repository
load("@@apple_support+//xcode:xcode_config.bzl", "xcode_config")

# buildifier: disable=canonical-repository
load("@@apple_support+//xcode:xcode_version.bzl", "xcode_version")

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

xcode_version(
    name = "version",
    default_ios_sdk_version = "18.2",
    default_macos_sdk_version = "15.2",
    default_tvos_sdk_version = "18.2",
    default_watchos_sdk_version = "11.2",
    version = "16.2.0.16C5032a",
)

xcode_config(
    name = "xcodes",
    default = ":version",
    versions = [":version"],
)

# buildifier: disable=canonical-repository
platform(
    name = "macos_exec",
    constraint_values = [
        "@@platforms//cpu:x86_64",
        "@@platforms//os:macos",
    ],
)
